title: "Pre-AGI AI Action Governance: Governing Autonomous Authority, Scale, and Consequential Action Before AGI"

type: software

authors:

* family-names: "Tan"
  given-names: "Sizhe"

repository-code: "https://github.com/sizhet/Pre-AGI-AI-Action-Governance"

url: "https://github.com/sizhet/Pre-AGI-AI-Action-Governance"

abstract: >-
Pre-AGI AI Action Governance is a research and policy framework for governing
consequential autonomous AI action without waiting for artificial general
intelligence. The framework shifts the primary governance focus from model
intelligence alone toward autonomous authority, access, scale, persistence,
external action, consequence, verification, and accountability. It introduces
the concepts of Scale-Looping Power, the Autonomous Impact Threshold,
the AI Action Accountability Stack, and the Governance Target Selection
Problem. Its central principle is that intelligence does not imply authority:
model evaluation should inform governance, action capability should trigger
governance, and consequence should determine governance intensity.

